Found under k331 (choices worker) and k335 (destroy worker), 2026-10-31, destroy lane:
- Destroy::_spec_worker_entries reads a pool's host for every provider. Since k331 validate() refuses host on a hetzner or local pool (neither reads it), but destroy does not validate: a hetzner pool's host shows up as a "Deleting X..." entry with no server id and deletes nothing; a local pool's host leads to an uninstall on 127.0.0.1 -- the machine ocp runs on.
- A control plane or pool skipped for an unknown or list provider is skipped without a word; when it is the only record, the run says "No nodes to destroy." (optional).
- cosmetic: a pool with host: 0 is listed as a machine named "0" and then left alone; apply reads it as no machine.

Fix: read host only where apply does (an ssh pool without a nodes: list), as worker_ocpnodes does; say a skipped entry on STDERR. Done = tests for the hetzner and local host cases (no entry, no uninstall on 127.0.0.1) and a line for a skipped entry.

Taken together with k331's red t/335 (2026-10-31): with k331 staged, validate() no longer gives a shape line for host on a hetzner/local pool, only the 'read for an ssh pool only' line, so t/335 test 4 ('a pool host of the wrong shape, whatever provider destroy knows') fails. k341 resolves it: destroy reads host only on ssh pools, so it no longer checks the shape on hetzner/local either (k323).

